== 10442 | Page 300 | {}
1015 am 26th  Grants Hd Qrs June 
City Point 930am 26th Qr Mr Genl ---- your dispatch of 
1130 am yesterday was recd by me at 9. 10 P
M ---- the only ocean Steamers in this river are
the "C Thomas", "Swanee", "Rebecca", "Barton" and
"Ellen S Terry" ---- I have given them the orders
you directed ---- they can carry an average of six
hundred men I have directed Col Biggs at Ft Monroe to
order the "City of Bath", "Cassandria", "Kent",
"Eastern City" Blackstone, "Constitution" and "Tilly". To
this list will probably be added the "Spaulding". he 
will report direct to you what they will carry ,
I do not know . I think that some of them
are still laden with forage and subsistence R. Ingalls
Chf Qr Mr 


545 pm  Grants Hd Qrs June 26
Hd Qrs City Point 4 pm 26th
for Gen Halleck ---- All is
quiet and our men resting
---- Sheridan is crossing the
river near Fort Powhattan
unmolested by the enemy 
---- Greggs loss was much
less than I was led

== 10450 | Page 308 | {}
2 pm  New York June 30th 1864
N York 30th June 1 pm ---- Qr Mr Genl
Wash The following steamers have sailed
for New Orleans "McClellan" 24 "Victor"
and "Karnack" 28 "Arago" 29
<deletion>nine</deletion> "Thomas A Scott" 30 ----
the "Merimack" arrives today & will
be sent back at once ----
the "Cahawba" has also arrived but
will require 6 days to repair
shall any more Steamers be sent
---- the "Mississippi" is expected in
4 or 5 days S Van Vliet
Qr Mr


1215 am July 1st  
N Orleans June twenty fourth for Col J. A.
Hardie Ins Genl Washn ---- I have telegd
to Genl Halleck & the Qr Mr Genl that nearly
all the locomotives & rolling stock for the
Vicksburg & Shreveport road can be procured here
---- The cost will be much less than 
they anticipate & it will in my opinion
be much more economical than any other kind
of land transportation & water transportation ---- the
occupation of the line of the Red River & the completion
of the road to Shreveport will give a new base for
operations against Texas sig Ed RS Canby Maj Genl

